# Trellis standard electrode map file format: (v.2)
# Previous map files should be backward comaptible with v.2
# <hardware.address>; <elec_group.elec_label>; <view.coords>
#
# Example: (for use with Ripple processor)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [processor.]port.FEslot.channel; [array.]electrode; [x.y.z]; [mapx, mapY, mapWidth, mapHeight]; [ImpedanceGreen, ImpedanceYellow, ImpedanceRed, Black]; [HeadX, HeadY, HeadWidth, HeadHeight, headOptions];
#
# '[x.y.z];' may be an empty whitespace string (ignored if 
# whitespace or empty)
# '[mapx, mapY, mapWidth, mapHeight];' must all be present together if used (along 
# with all previous columns)
# mapX, mapY uses a cartesian coordinate system as seen below(map will automatically 
# scale/translate the map coordinates based off the min/max map cordinates provided)
#                   Y+
#                   |
#              X- --+-- X+
#                   |
#                   Y-
# [ImpedanceGreen, ImpedanceYellow, ImpedanceRed, ImpedanceBlack] must all be present 
# together if used (along with all previous columns). Once included, all 
# subsequent electrodes will use the same values until changed.
#
# Multiple heads (ellipes) may optionally be defined. Head options are as followed (must be a single string with any combination of the following):
# V : Draw a vertical line from top of ellipse to bottom
# H : Draw a Horizontal line from left to right of Ellipse
# U : Draw a nose facing upward
# D : Draw a nose facing downward
# R : Draw a nose facing right
# L : Draw a nose facing left
#
# NOTE: all fields are 1-indexed and any whitespace will be ignored
#       terminating semicolon (;) is optional
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

